    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Spelling and special sounds",
     "texto": [
      "When spelling in Dutch, you will often come across the digraph «ij» (called «lange ij», to distinguish it from «ei» or «korte ei»). When a letter appears twice in a row, you say «dubbel» (for example, «dubbel o» for double o). If you don't understand how a personal detail is spelled, you can politely ask: «Kunt u dat spellen?» (Can you spell that?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
